From ff224cf4107874518d646f0c1a0f01a472ecc07e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: itkadr-git <itkadr-git@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:31:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(myrmidon): enable merge_group checks for merge queue
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

main went red twice on 06.10 by stitching PRs that were each green on
their own: between a green PR head and the merge, main moved. Teach the
CI and the review gate about the GitHub merge queue so every candidate
commit is re-checked on top of fresh main before it lands.

- myrmidon-ci.yml: add the merge_group (checks_requested) trigger; plan
  and tests-affected diff merge_group.base_sha..head_sha so the tier and
  the affected tests match the PR inside the group; never auto-cancel a
  queue run (a cancelled run would evict the group from the queue);
  ci-result keeps the same names, so main-protection is satisfied on the
  candidate.
- myrmidon-hot-files-review.yml: fire on merge_group but only report
  hot-files-review as success on the candidate commit — review is
  enforced on the PR, the queue must not wait on it.
- docs/myrmidon/merge-queue.md + .ru.md: how the queue works, what CI
  does on a queue event, the reviewer (review-approved) and steward
  (gh pr merge --auto) roles, and what to do when a PR drops out.
- change fragment docs/myrmidon/changes/1-6-5-merge-queue-workflows.md,
- docs index row in docs/myrmidon/README.md.

Co-Authored-By: Paperclip <noreply@paperclip.ing>
